Terminal 3 (code: T3) – or Taj Mahal Terminal or T3C – opened at Delhi Indira Gandhi International Airport on July 4, 2009.^{[1]} Although it has been operational since 2009, it became the primary airport terminal for international departures, arrivals, passenger, cargo and ground transport on 25th August 2012 on completion of the relocation process.^{[2]}

The terminal is approximately 530,000 m^{2} in area and has a 5 km perimeter length housing 18 aerobridges (including 3 double-crossovers).^{[3]} Terminal 3 operates 24 hours a day with an annual capacity of 22.5 million passengers. It features separate facilities to departing and arriving international passengers. The first floor houses the departures area with the second floor being dedicated to arrivals. The terminal can operate the A380 aircraft with 628 seats.^{[4]}

